SecureARC is a high-performance ARC (Authenticated Received Chain) milter
implementing RFC 8617. It validates existing ARC chains on inbound mail and
seals messages with new ARC sets for forwarding.

Features:
- ARC chain validation (ARC-Authentication-Results, ARC-Message-Signature,
  ARC-Seal) with full cryptographic verification
- ARC sealing with RSA-SHA256 signing
- Thread-per-core architecture with kqueue I/O multiplexing
- ZMQ event publishing for monitoring and reporting
- Multi-listener support (verify/seal/both modes per listener)
